  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 220 PM CST Thu Nov 26 2026\n\nSeasonably mild temperatures settle across Iowa next week with highs \nin the 40s and 50s. Zonal flow sets up across the area with only \nmodest variability in temperatures day to day. Zonal flow also \nkeeps moisture transport out of the area and the forecast is \ndry for much of the upcoming week. Late in the week models \nsuggest a more robust western US trough will develop into a \ncut off upper level low that will move across the central US. \nThat will bring the next notable chance for precipitation to \nIowa.",
